The Seven Padārthas
The Vaiśeṣika school of philosophy recognises seven padārthas or categories of realities. ‘Padārtha’ means ‘what is denoted by a word’, an object of knowledge. All such objects can be divided into two classes: भाव (being) and अभाव (non-being). भाव stands for all the positive and existent realities whereas अभाव denotes negative facts (Vaiśeṣikasūtras
